    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the road entrance to the driveway so responders can identify the property quickly at night or in low visibility.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with reflective posts on both sides to define the opening for large emergency vehicles.\n• Keep the full width of the access drive clear of parked vehicles, equipment, and landscaping to allow two-way movement for emergency vehicles.\n• Maintain the circular driveway free of obstacles so arriving units can pull forward and turn around without backing out onto the road.\n• Identify and mark any alternate rear access point across the open terrain so responders are not limited to the single front driveway.\n• Keep any perimeter fence gates accessible and unlocked, or provide a lock box with a standardized key, so responders can reach the rear of the property without delay.\n• Post the property address on the residence itself in numbers visible from the driveway approach.\n• Designate a clear staging area on the circular driveway or adjacent open space where command and support vehicles can park without blocking the access drive.\n• Trim any landscaping along the access drive that narrows the usable width or reduces sight lines for approaching vehicles."
  },
