    "recommendations": "• Trim shrubs that are growing directly next to the structure.\n• Remove dead or dry grass from within a few feet of the structure's base.\n• Thin scattered trees near the structure to increase open space between tree canopy and the building.\n• Clear brush from the edges of the driveway to keep the single access route open for vehicles.\n• Keep overhanging tree branches trimmed back from above the driveway.\n• Remove dense brush patches closest to the structure before dry season.\n• Mow or cut ground vegetation in the area immediately surrounding the structure.\n• Separate shrub groupings near any outbuildings or fences connected to the main structure.\n• Keep the single access route clear of fallen branches and overgrown vegetation along its full length.\n• Cut back shrubs along the driveway entry point to maintain clear sightlines for entering and exiting vehicles."
